  "title": "Shaka kaSenzangakhona",
  "summary": "Shaka was the son of Senzangakhona and Nandi and served in the army of the Mthethwa chief Dingiswayo. He claimed the Zulu throne in 1816, standardised a short stabbing spear and large shield, and imposed strict discipline. His conquests helped trigger the Mfecane. He was killed in September 1828 by half-brothers including Dingane, who succeeded him.",
